  <section class="wrap fiche-body">
    <div>
      <h2>The vibe</h2>
      <p>Colibri'Vet, also in Sainte-Maxime, offers physiotherapy sessions for animals alongside regular consultations, as well as a wider range of services according to the official website: hydrotherapy, imaging (X-ray/ultrasound), herbal medicine, elective surgery, hospitalisation, lab work and tailored nutritional advice.</p>

      <h2>What to know before you go</h2>
      <p>The clinic is open Monday to Friday, 9am-12:30pm and 3pm-6:30pm, and closed on Saturday and Sunday. Hours are confirmed by two independent sources (the official site colibrivet.fr and monrendezvousveto.fr), correcting an earlier, less reliable version mentioning Saturday-morning opening. Outside these hours, emergencies are redirected to UVDelta 83, so Colibri'Vet does not handle them itself.</p>
      <p>Physiotherapy can be useful alongside a treatment or as part of rehabilitation after an injury, surgery, or for an older dog. Online reviews praise the welcome, professionalism and speed of care, though no numeric rating was found. Physiotherapy prices aren't published — ask directly.</p>
      <div class="callout">Coco's tip: if your dog is recovering from an injury or getting older and stiffer, ask whether the physiotherapy offered here could help.</div>

      <h2>Nearby</h2>
      <p>Sainte-Maxime and its seafront are close by.</p>
